{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_13a",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_13a_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_10",
      "quote": "A total of 13 studies were therefore included in our qualitative synthesis [14-26]. Of these studies, 10 were included in our quantitative synthesis [14, 15, 19-26].",
      "reason": "The manuscript reports which studies entered the qualitative and quantitative syntheses and, in Results text, implicitly explains inclusion per synthesis via outcome availability (e.g. 'The primary outcome of first pass ETI success was chosen for this analysis as overall ETI success was not fully reported in two of the prehospital studies without video technology'). However, the Methods section does not explicitly describe a process (e.g. tabulating study intervention characteristics against planned synthesis groups) used to decide eligibility for each synthesis; such information appears only retrospectively in Results."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 70
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_13b",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_13b_e1",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence describes data extraction items (text_5) and statistical analysis methods (text_8, e.g., dichotomous outcomes analysed as risk ratios), but nowhere describes data preparation methods such as handling of missing summary statistics or data conversions. Text_8 addresses analysis, not data preparation; the manuscript notes some studies did not fully report outcomes (text_11) but never explains how missing data were handled."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 85
